# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is tracked.
# Never commit a real token.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mapbox — public access token (pk.*)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The ONLY token this project needs. Read at runtime and passed to
# Mapbox.setAccessToken() in src/lib/mapbox.ts.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* is deliberate: this value is embedded in the JS bundle and is
# extractable from any shipped build. That is fine for a pk.* token — it is
# public by design. Do NOT protect it by hiding it; protect it in the Mapbox
# dashboard with URL restrictions and a minimal scope set.
#
# Create at: https://console.mapbox.com/account/access-tokens/
EXPO_PUBLIC_MAPBOX_TOKEN=pk.your_public_token_here


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mapbox — secret download token (sk.*)  ::  NOT NEEDED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately absent. Mapbox dropped the download-token requirement, and
# @rnmapbox/maps 10.3.5 marks it deprecated in both the config plugin and the
# podspec ("Download token is no longer required by Mapbox. Do not set this.").
#
# Most tutorials still tell you to put an sk.* token in .netrc,
# gradle.properties, or a MAPBOX_DOWNLOADS_TOKEN EAS secret. Skip all of that —
# it is the single most common source of stale-tutorial build breakage.
#
# The legacy escape hatch, only if a future Mapbox change reinstates the
# requirement, is the RNMAPBOX_MAPS_DOWNLOAD_TOKEN environment variable. Do not
# set RNMapboxMapsDownloadToken in app.json — that writes the secret into
# Podfile and gradle.properties, both of which are committed.
